  - The key rule is: Survive.  Dead characters accomplish little.

  - Read the Guidebook again.
  - Read the story of Krysia's Krusader (available on the web and in the
    RGRN archive in Google Groups.)
  - Use the '/' command for every new creature/item.

  - Try on every non-cursed piece of armor you find for AC.  
    - Your pet can tell you which are non-cursed.  
    - AC is passive 
      - Doesn't require you to think.
      - Works on every monster when surrounded.
      - There's no better place to allocate carrying capacity than 
        defense.
    - You scrabble through every bit of armor you find in order to live
      long enough to scrabble through more armor.
  - Elbereth!
  - Kill things from a distance (See my signature.)  
    - "Throw rocks at it!"
    - "Run up and hit something" is the best way to die.
    - Think of ranged attacks as perfect AC on your part.
  - Use your pet.  
    - Learn to lead your pet.  If your pet won't follow you, you need to
      follow it.  
    - Develop your pet: Let is get weaker monsters.  A large dog/cat can
      handle almost anything in the mines or up to Sokoban.
  - Do NOT be burdened.  Learn to stash early and often.
  - Every role is different.  Different weapons, different skills, 
    different strengths, different weaknesses.
    - Which weapon skill(s) to enhance can be critical.


  Summary:  Let your pet get it.  Elbereth.  Ranged attacks.  Better
armor.  Better armor.  Better armor.


